    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Take-off \u0026 Landing\nTERRE\nStart und landung\nDécollage et atterissage\nAl salir y aterrizar\nBefore opening an exit,\nquickly look through a\nwindow to check outside\nfor the following:\nSmoke\nIf smoke is so thick you can not see out,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nFire\nIf there is fire outside the aircraft,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nDebris/\nObstructions\nIf there is metal debris or obstructions,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nEmergency exits\n**0\n·3w0\n871 47\nNotausgang\nSorties de secours\nSalidas de emergencia\nA\nB\nA\nDirect passengers\naway from aircraft.\nNo smoking\nNicht rauchen\nDéfense de fumer\nNo fumar\nA\nEXIT\nExit\n#*0\nHO\nAusgang\nSortie\nSalida\nB\n2\n2\nOxygen\nsauerstoff\nOxygène\nOxigeno\nCheck that the slide has properly\ninflated and is in good condition.\nUse handles to stabilize slide.\n1.....P",
      "CA 344 4/91\nPrinted in the U.S.A.\n2008.055,857",
      "Safety\nSicherheit\nSécurité\nSeguridad\nB-B7\nUNITED\nIf you are sitting in an exit row\nand you can not read this card\nor can not see well enough to\nfollow these instructions,\nplease tell a crew member.\n67461298\nWenn sie neben einem ausgang sitzen und sie verstehen\nkein Englisch, bitte verständigen sie die flugzeugbesatzung.\nSi vous êtes assis dans une rangée de sieges à côté\nd'une sortie, et vous ne comprenez pas la langue\nanglaise, veuillez le dire à un membre de l'équipage.\nSi usted se encuentra sentado/a en una fila de asientos\na la par de una salida u usted no entiende el idioma\ninglés, favor de avisarle a un tripulante.\nEmergency exits are often heavy, awkward to lift, push,\npull, and maneuver when opening. Because of this, and\nfor the safety of all passengers, Federal Law requires\nthat we only seat qualified passengers next to exits.\nIf you are sitting in an exit row, you may be asked to\nopen the exit and assist our crew in the event of an\nemergency. Please ask to be reseated if you:\n•Have a physical condition which may not be visible and\nwhich may prevent you from helping.\n•Think you lack the strength, mobility, dexterity, or\nbalance required to open the exit and assist our crew.\n•Do not think you could reach the exit, open it, and get\nout quickly.\n•Believe the physical exertion required to open the exit\nwould injure you.\n•Are hearing impaired and could not hear commands\nfrom our crew.\n•Are not able to give oral commands to others.\n•Do not understand the instructions in this brochure.\n•Have other responsibilities (such as a small child to\ncare for) which would prevent you from helping.\n•Are less than 15 years old.\n•Do not wish to help in this way.\nFederal regulations require all passengers,\nregardless of where they are sitting or their physical\ncondition, to review this card, for their safety.\nFollow these instructions, the directions of crew\nmembers, and placarded signs.\nWhen finished reviewing this card please return it\nto the seat pocket for our next customer."
    ],
